{%- doc -%}
  A detail card on the product page (Figma: Standart Product Page → Estimated
  Shipping, Ingredients & Allergens, Storage).

  [ui-panel] draws the plate, the glyph and the disclosure; this composes what goes
  inside one — the line that stays visible, the rule that appears on opening, the
  copy under it, and the lines when the card carries lines instead of prose.

  It lives in the kit because two callers draw the same card: [_ui-product-panel],
  which is what a merchant arranges in the theme editor, and [_ui-product-panels],
  which draws one per `detail_panel` metaobject entry when a product carries its
  own. One composition, so the two cannot drift.

  @param {string} title - The card's heading.
  @param {string} [icon] - Icon asset name. `none` is treated as no icon.
  @param {string} [summary] - The line that stays visible when the card is shut.
  @param {string} [body] - The copy opening the card reveals.
  @param {string} [rows] - Captured `ui-detail-line` markup, for a card of lines.
  @param {boolean} [collapsible] - Lets the card open. Ignored when there is no body.
  @param {string} [padding] - `default` or `tight`, passed to ui-panel.
  @param {string} [attributes] - Extra HTML attributes for the card's root.

  @example
  {% render 'ui-detail-card', title: 'Storage', icon: 'thermometer', summary: lede, body: full, collapsible: true %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign card_icon = icon
  if card_icon == 'none'
    assign card_icon = ''
  endif

  # A card with nothing behind the caret does not get one: a disclosure that opens
  # onto an empty box is a control that visibly does nothing.
  assign is_collapsible = false
  if collapsible and body != blank
    assign is_collapsible = true
  endif
-%}

{%- capture card_intro -%}
  {%- if summary != blank -%}
    <p class="ui-detail-card__intro">{{ summary }}</p>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture card_body -%}
  {%- if is_collapsible -%}
    <div class="ui-detail-card__rule" role="separator"></div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if body != blank -%}
    <div class="ui-detail-card__body">{{ body }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if rows != blank -%}
    <div class="ui-detail-card__rows">{{ rows }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

{% render 'ui-panel',
  title: title,
  icon: card_icon,
  intro: card_intro,
  body: card_body,
  collapsible: is_collapsible,
  animated: true,
  padding: padding,
  class: 'ui-detail-card',
  attributes: attributes
%}

{% stylesheet %}
  .ui-detail-card__intro,
  .ui-detail-card__body {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ui-color-black);
    font-family: var(--ui-font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: var(--ui-font-body-weight);
    line-height: var(--ui-line-height);
  }

  /*
   * Descendant, not child: the two callers hand over slightly different markup.
   * A theme-editor card gives bare paragraphs, while a metaobject card arrives
   * wrapped in the div `metafield_tag` draws around it, which would put the
   * paragraphs a level out of reach of a child selector.
   */
  .ui-detail-card__body :where(p, ul, ol, h2, h3, h4, blockquote) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .ui-detail-card__body :where(p, ul, ol, h2, h3, h4, blockquote) + * {
    margin-block-start: 1em;
  }

  .ui-detail-card__rule {
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--ui-color-light-blue);
  }

  .ui-detail-card__rows {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
